# The same board, which reaches into its charts: it makes each chart's figure (`self.left.create_figure()`) and plots on
# the chart's axes itself (`self.left.ax.plot(..)`). Each call runs on the board through the field of the chart it reads
# (#172), so each figure rests in that part of the board, and the screen shows two, as on the clean side. What differs is
# who decides: here the board's own code reads its charts' axes, and the charts have no `line` of their own.

